Interfaces and invariants to document:

```
initialize(catalog: Dictionary, runtime: Dictionary) -> {ok, error_code}
  # First passes through ConfigGate.can_start_economy; illegal → rejected, no default backfill.
commit_catch(state: GameState, catch_event_id: String, species_id: String, caught_at_utc: String) -> {ok, code, instance_id?}
  # Validation: catch_event_id is non-empty and not in processed_catch_ids; species_id is in catalog;
  # basket.size() < basket_capacity; caught_at_utc is a non-empty string.
  # Generate instance: instance_id="fish-"+catch_event_id, sale_price_at_catch = catalog's base_price snapshot.
  # Success: basket += fish, processed_catch_ids += id, revision += 1.
  # Same id with different parameters re-submitted → CONFLICT_CATCH_PARAMS (not disguised by AlreadyApplied, INTERFACES §5).
sell_fish(state: GameState, sale_event_id: String, instance_ids: Array) -> {ok, code, gold_added?}
  # Validation: sale_event_id is a non-empty string; instance_ids is an array of non-empty strings with no duplicates;
  # all exist in basket; if sale_event_id is in processed_sale_ids with identical parameters → AlreadyApplied (gold 0, no mutation);
  # gold_added = Σ sale_price_at_catch (integer ≥ 0).
  # Success: atomically remove fish + wallet_gold += gold_added + processed_sale_ids += id, revision += 1.
can_settle_catch(state) / capacity check is implicit.
```

Error codes: NOT_INITIALIZED, NULL_GAME_STATE, BAD_EVENT_ID (empty/non-string), UNKNOWN_SPECIES, BASKET_FULL (capacity), ALREADY_APPLIED, CONFLICT_CATCH_PARAMS, CONFLICT_SALE_PARAMS, UNKNOWN_INSTANCE, DUP_INSTANCE_ID (duplicate within request), BAD_INSTANCE_LIST (non-array/non-string/empty), NEGATIVE_GOLD impossible (price validated ≥0) — assert wallet_gold ≥ 0 always.

Also maintain an in-memory ledger of processed request fingerprints (catch id → species+price, sale id → sorted instance ids + gold) for conflict detection; note as a boundary: in-memory only, SAVE-001 will persist or reconstruct it in its scope; conflict detection after restart is a SAVE-001 handover.

Important: ECO-001 does zero file writes, does not touch user:// (in-memory tests only per the queue minimum "memory tests"). Save integration is SAVE-001.

