Interfaces:

```
class_name EconomyService extends RefCounted
initialize(catalog: Dictionary, runtime: Dictionary) -> {ok, error_code}
  # First passes through ConfigGate.can_start_economy; on failure, zero side effects (follows FSM-001 initialize's form)
set_persistence_gate(gate: Callable) -> {ok, code}  # default is always-ok in-memory gate; SAVE-001 injects the real atomic save
commit_catch(state: GameState, catch_event_id: String, species_id: String, caught_at_utc: String) -> {ok, code, instance_id, gold_delta=0}
sell_fish(state: GameState, sale_event_id: String, instance_ids: Array) -> {ok, code, gold_added}
processed_catch_count(state) / processed_sale_count(state) / snapshot_ledger() -> Dictionary (in-memory fingerprint ledger, for tests and SAVE-001)
```

Error codes (stable strings):
NOT_INITIALIZED, NULL_GAME_STATE, BAD_EVENT_ID, UNKNOWN_SPECIES, BASKET_FULL, ALREADY_APPLIED, CONFLICT_CATCH_PARAMS, CONFLICT_SALE_PARAMS, UNKNOWN_INSTANCE, BAD_INSTANCE_LIST (non-array / empty array / non-string element / empty string), DUP_INSTANCE_IN_REQUEST, BAD_TIMESTAMP, BAD_PRICE_SNAPSHOT (catalog price invalid — but ConfigGate already prevents this, as a secondary defense line).

Invariants:
- Pure RefCounted data layer, no Node/_process, no user://, no file writes (ECO-001's in-memory tests are the minimum acceptance criterion; save writes are SAVE-001).
- GameState is the single authority: economy is the only module allowed to write wallet_gold/basket/processed_*_ids/revision (this ticket); FSM/UI only read.
- All commands "validate first → construct new state → (persistence gate) → bulk commit": failure paths have zero side effects (basket/gold/revision/processed ids all unchanged).
- Idempotency: same catch_event_id/sale_event_id + same parameters → ALREADY_APPLIED, state changes at most once; same ID with different parameters → CONFLICT_* and logged in in-memory log (INTERFACES §5, don't cover it up).
- instance_id = "fish-" + catch_event_id (each catch event settles at most 1 fish → structurally unique; reproducible in deterministic tests; doesn't depend on UUID randomness).
- sale_price_at_catch is snapshotted at commit_catch from the current catalog's base_price; subsequent changes to catalog/gold do not retroactively apply.
- wallet_gold is always a non-negative integer; gold_added = Σ instance.sale_price_at_catch (first dedupe per request then sum, duplicates within a request → DUP_INSTANCE_IN_REQUEST reject).
- Each successful commit does revision += 1 (monotonic).
- Full basket: commit_catch rejects with BASKET_FULL when basket.size() >= capacity (double insurance: FSM request_cast already has a gate; if a settlement arrives after the basket became full, explicit reject, don't lose fish, don't exceed capacity — schema $comment basket ≤ capacity).
- Serial: EconomyService's methods are synchronous, single-threaded, one command at a time; UI/Controller (later ticket) must go through this service as the sole booking entry, no concurrent writes to GameState.
- Don't change economic parameters: 20/60/30/10 and prices/weights are read-only; runner has value-lock re-check.
- Class names are new: FishInstance/EconomyService are unused (measured: 15 class_name).

Test matrix E1–E10:
- E1 Full-basket cast block + post-sale recovery (FSM integration): basket with 9 fish → request_cast ok → commit 1 fish → basket 10 → request_cast rejected with BASKET_FULL (no RNG consumption) → sell 1 fish → request_cast ok again (T-ECO-01)
- E2 catch idempotency: retry same catch_event_id 100 times → exactly 1 fish enters basket, processed_catch_ids has exactly 1 entry, revision increases by exactly 1 (T-ECO-02)
- E3 sale idempotency: retry same sale_event_id 100 times → gold increases exactly once, sold instances don't re-appear, basket count is stable (T-ECO-03)
- E4 Error matrix (T-ECO-04): sell with non-existent instance id; duplicate instance id within same request; sell with empty array; non-string elements; catch with invalid species_id; empty/invalid event id; catch after full; all return stable codes and zero state change; assert wallet_gold >= 0 and never negative throughout
- E5 Same-ID different-params conflict: 2nd commit_catch with same catch_event_id but different species → CONFLICT_CATCH_PARAMS, gold/basket unchanged, in-memory log recorded; same for 2nd sell with different instance list → CONFLICT_SALE_PARAMS (INTERFACES §5)
- E6 Price snapshot: after committing 1 fish, change catalog's base_price copy → sell still adds gold at sale_price_at_catch (SDD 2026-11-11 ruling)
- E7 Failure-path zero side effects: for each error code in E4/E5, snapshot GameState (deep-copy compare) before and after → match field-by-field
- E8 Integration: FSM full cycle → produce_catch_candidate → commit_catch(species, event id) → 1 fish in basket, source_event_id=event_id, instance_id="fish-"+id; ack_settlement→IDLE→re-cast (V01-E01/E02, FSM R-3 handover re-check)
- E9 Value-lock: assert data==examples value-match + config 20/60/30/10 + 3 fish prices 8/16/32 unchanged (R-4 precedent)
- E10 persistence-gate failure path: inject an always-false gate → commit_catch/sell_fish return PERSIST_FAILED and GameState unchanged (advance booking for SAVE-001's "only publish after save succeeds", this ticket does not write to disk)

